From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 22:03:07 +0200
Subject: nfc: nxp-nci: Complete proprietary command requests

nxp_nci_post_setup() sends NXP_ACT_PROP_EXTN with nci_prop_cmd(), a
synchronous request. The generic NCI core routes the proprietary (GID
0xF) response to the driver's prop_ops table, but the driver registered
none, so the response was logged as "unsupported rsp opcode 0xf02" and
the request was never completed. It then blocked until the command
timeout (~5 s), delaying every bring-up, spamming
wait_for_completion...failed, and leaving the request machinery in a bad
state for the commands that followed.

Register a prop_ops handler that completes the request with the
controller's status byte, the same way the fdp driver does. Bring-up no
longer stalls and the proprietary configuration is applied cleanly.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c | 24 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
@@ -277,6 +277,28 @@ static const struct nci_driver_ops nxp_nci_core_ops[] = {
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * Complete the request for a proprietary command. The generic core has
+ * no handler for a proprietary (GID 0xF) response, so without this the
+ * command sent from .post_setup never completes and blocks bring-up for
+ * a full command timeout.
+ */
+static int nxp_nci_prop_rsp(struct nci_dev *ndev, struct sk_buff *skb)
+{
+	__u8 status = skb->data[0];
+
+	nci_req_complete(ndev, status);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct nci_driver_ops nxp_nci_prop_ops[] = {
+	{
+		/* NXP_ACT_PROP_EXTN */
+		.opcode = nci_opcode_pack(NCI_GID_PROPRIETARY, 0x02),
+		.rsp = nxp_nci_prop_rsp,
+	},
+};
+
 static const struct nci_ops nxp_nci_ops = {
 	.open = nxp_nci_open,
 	.close = nxp_nci_close,
@@ -286,6 +308,8 @@ static const struct nci_ops nxp_nci_ops = {
 	.get_rfprotocol = nxp_nci_get_rfprotocol,
 	.core_ops = nxp_nci_core_ops,
 	.n_core_ops = ARRAY_SIZE(nxp_nci_core_ops),
+	.prop_ops = nxp_nci_prop_ops,
+	.n_prop_ops = ARRAY_SIZE(nxp_nci_prop_ops),
 };
 
 int nxp_nci_probe(void *phy_id, struct device *pdev,
-- 
